{"scope":"rt-67b51547af","css":".rt-67b51547af p.MsoNormal, .rt-67b51547af li.MsoNormal, .rt-67b51547af div.MsoNormal {margin:0cm; font-size:10.0pt; font-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif;}\n.rt-67b51547af div.WordSection1 {}","html":"<div class=WordSection1>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span lang=EN-US>.<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span style='position:relative;z-index:251657728;left:-117px;\r\ntop:30px;width:1143px;height:32px'><img width=914 height=2\r\nsrc=\"data:image\/gif;base64,R0lGODlhdwQCAHcAMSH+GlNvZnR3YXJlOiBNaWNyb3NvZnQgT2ZmaWNlACH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAB3BAIAgAAAAAAAAAJLBHKJq83vIpyy0msz3rrz74XgKJbkaaboqrbs68bwLNf0bef4rvf87wsCh8Ii8ZgyIJfGJvPpjEKn0ir1as1it9ou9+sNg8fiMqUAADs=\"><\/span><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:14.0pt;\r\nfont-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<br clear=ALL>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><u><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:14.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>DEPARTMENT\r\nOF PATHOLOGY<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><u><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'><span\r\n style='text-decoration:none'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HEPATITIS B\r\nVIRUS - VIRAL LOAD (QUANTITATIVE) : REAL TIME PCR<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:4.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<table class=MsoNormalTable border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0 width=748\r\n style='width:561.05pt;margin-left:5.4pt;border-collapse:collapse'>\r\n <tr style='height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <td width=290 valign=top style='width:217.3pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Test name<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=195 valign=top style='width:146.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><u><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Result<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=85 valign=top style='width:63.8pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Unit<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=178 valign=top style='width:133.55pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><u><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Bio. Ref. Interval<\/span><\/u><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <td width=290 valign=top style='width:217.3pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:10.5pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HEPATITIS B VIRAL DNA<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=195 valign=top style='width:146.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:10.5pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>TARGET NOT\r\n  DETECTED<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=85 valign=top style='width:63.8pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;text-autospace:none'><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>IU\/mL<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=178 valign=top style='width:133.55pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <td width=290 valign=top style='width:217.3pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Methodology:\r\n  Real Time Multiplex PCR<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=195 valign=top style='width:146.4pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=85 valign=top style='width:63.8pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=178 valign=top style='width:133.55pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:26.1pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>RESULTS INTERPRETATION<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<table class=MsoNormalTable border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0\r\n style='margin-left:5.4pt;border-collapse:collapse;border:none'>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=351 valign=top style='width:263.25pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>RESULT in IU\/mL REMARKS<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=358 valign=top style='width:268.65pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-left:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>RESULT in IU\/mL REMARKS<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=351 valign=top style='width:263.25pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Target\r\n  not detected <\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=358 valign=top style='width:268.65pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Likely\r\n  below the lower limit of linear range of the assay<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=351 valign=top style='width:263.25pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&lt;20<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=358 valign=top style='width:268.65pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HBV DNA\r\n  detected, but below the lower limit of linear range of the assay These\r\n  results should be interpreted with caution<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=351 valign=top style='width:263.25pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&gt;=20 to 1\r\n  x109<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=358 valign=top style='width:268.65pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HBV DNA\r\n  detected within the linear range of the assay<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td width=351 valign=top style='width:263.25pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  border-top:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&gt;1 x 109<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=358 valign=top style='width:268.65pt;border-top:none;border-left:\r\n  none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;\r\n  padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>HBV DNA\r\n  detected above the linear range of the assay<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>COMMENTS<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>1.Linear\r\nreporting range of the assay is 20 - 1 x 10^9 IU\/mL<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2. Conversion\r\nfactor: 1 IU\/mL = 5.82 copies \/mL<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>3.Test conducted\r\non Serum \/ Plasma<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>4.This test is\r\nnot intended for use as a screening test for the presence of HBV in blood or\r\nblood products or as a diagnostic test to confirm \u00a0<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0\u00a0 the presence\r\nof HBV infection<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>5.HBV genotyping\r\nand Drug resistance is recommended in positive cases if value is &gt;2000\r\nIU\/mL.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>6.A &quot;<b>DETECTED<\/b>&quot;\r\nresult will be reported with quantification in IU\/ml. It indicates the degree\r\nif active HBV viral replication in the patient.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>A &quot;LESS THAN\r\nDETECTABLE LIMIT&quot; result indicates that either absence of HBV DNA in\r\npatient\u2019s specimen or HBV DNA level is below the lower limit of quantification\r\nof this <\/span><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>assay.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:7.0pt;font-family:\"Arial\",sans-serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>CLINICAL\r\nRELEVANCE<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Hepatitis B Virus\r\n(HBV) is a member of Hepa DNA virus family transmitted primarily by body fluids\r\nespecially serum; sexual transmission and transmission from mother to baby.\r\nMajority of the infected individuals recover completely; about 1-2% have\r\npersistent viral replication leading to chronic hepatitis. Frequency of chronic\r\nHBV infection is 5-10% in immunocompromised patients and 80% in neonates.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>CLINICAL\r\nAPPLICATION<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>1.Monitoring\r\nresponse to therapy in chronic HBV infection<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2.Predict\r\nresponse to favourable treatment outcome<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>3.valuable tool\r\nwhen used in conjunction with other serological markers in the management of\r\nHBV infection<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:8.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>LIMITATIONS<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>1.This test can\r\nquantitate\/detect Hepatitis B Virus DNA over the range 20- 1X10^9 IU\/mL.\r\nHowever this does not mean that lower copies or higher copies cannot be<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>detected. The\r\nlower copies can be detected in some cases. This is a limitation of the\r\ncurrently available extraction systems.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2.Patients\r\nsuffering from chronic HBV infection typically have intermittent viraemia.\r\nSamples collected during the non- viraemic phase may test negative despite the\r\npresence<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>of active\r\ninfection. Hence, in such cases where HBV PCR is negative despite strong\r\nclinical suspicion, a repeat sample collected at an interval of two weeks from\r\nthe initial<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>sample is\r\nstrongly recommended to rule out active disease.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>3. The result of\r\nthis test must always be correlated with clinical status and history of the\r\npatient and other relevant data and should not be used alone for the\r\ninterpretation.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:6.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>4. Although all\r\nprecautions are taken during molecular genetic tests, the currently available\r\ndata indicate that the technical error in molecular DNA analysis is\r\napproximately<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:5.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2%. It is\r\nimportant that all clinicians or persons requesting Molecular Diagnostic\r\ntesting are aware of these data before acting upon the results.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:5.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>5. The results\r\nassume that the sample is provided from this patient only and that all patient\r\ninformation provided is correct.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"157.5pt 18.0pt 72.0pt 40.5pt"}}